  "worked_solution": "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nE\u2227(E\u2228F)\u2261E.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\u2227(F\u2228E) & \u2261F\u2262E.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $E.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E\u2227(F\u2228E) & \u2261E\u2227(E\u2228F) \\\\  & \u2261E.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $E.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
